    "## 7. Hyperband — Compute-Efficient Hyperparameter Search\n",
    "\n",
    "### The hyperparameter tuning problem\n",
    "\n",
    "You have $A$ candidate configurations (e.g., different $\\rho$ values, learning rates, architectures). Each requires a full training run to evaluate. If each run takes 2 days and $A = 8$, that's 16 compute-days.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Successive halving (Hyperband's core idea)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Intuition:** bad models fail fast. Run all candidates briefly, drop the bottom half, give the survivors twice as many steps. Repeat.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Round 1: Run A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H for T steps → drop worst half\n",
    "Round 2: Run A, C, E, G for 2T steps             → drop worst half\n",
    "Round 3: Run A, C for 4T steps                   → drop worst half\n",
    "Round 4: Run A for 8T steps                      → winner!\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Compute efficiency:** total compute ≈ $2A \\cdot T$ instead of $A \\cdot T_{\\max}$. Roughly halved, with exponentially more resources devoted to promising configs.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key property:** you continue training — you don't restart from scratch at each round. Compute invested in eliminated models is \"wasted\" but the fraction is bounded.\n",
    "\n",
    "> 📌 *Lecture:* \"Better models are going to receive exponentially more compute. Every round better models are getting more and more data. This very simple idea did a huge huge service because you could do very complicated things in tuning. That simple trick is one that I use kind of all the time.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "### When Hyperband beats grid search / random search\n",
    "\n",
    "- When training is expensive (GPU-hours)\n",
    "- When the learning curve of bad models diverges early\n",
    "- When you have many hyperparameters to search over\n",
    "\n",
    "### In practice\n",
    "\n",
    "Modern libraries that implement Hyperband: `Ray Tune`, `Optuna`, `Keras Tuner`, `HuggingFace Trainer`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "np.random.seed(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Simulate 8 configs with different \"true\" final performance + noisy learning curves\n",
    "n_configs = 8\n",
    "T_max = 64  # max steps\n",
    "\n",
    "# Each config has a true final MSE (some are good, some are bad)\n",
    "true_final = np.array([0.25, 2.5, 0.35, 3.0, 0.40, 1.8, 0.30, 4.0])\n",
    "labels = list('ABCDEFGH')\n",
    "\n",
    "def learning_curve(config_idx, t):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Simulate MSE at step t for config.\"\"\"\n",
    "    final = true_final[config_idx]\n",
    "    # MSE decays exponentially toward final value\n",
    "    decay = np.exp(-t / 20) * (5 - final)\n",
    "    noise = np.random.normal(0, 0.05)\n",
    "    return final + decay + noise\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run Hyperband-style successive halving\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 4, figsize=(14, 4), sharey=True)\n",
    "survivors = list(range(n_configs))\n",
    "t_start = 0\n",
    "t_budgets = [4, 8, 16, 32]\n",
    "\n",
    "colors_cfg = plt.cm.tab10(np.linspace(0, 1, n_configs))\n",
    "t_cumulative = np.zeros(n_configs)\n",
    "\n",
    "for round_idx, budget in enumerate(t_budgets):\n",
    "    ax = axes[round_idx]\n",
    "    scores = {}\n",
    "    for cfg in survivors:\n",
    "        steps = np.arange(t_cumulative[cfg], t_cumulative[cfg] + budget + 1, 1)\n",
    "        mses = [learning_curve(cfg, t) for t in steps]\n",
    "        ax.plot(steps, mses, color=colors_cfg[cfg], linewidth=2, label=labels[cfg])\n",
    "        t_cumulative[cfg] += budget\n",
    "        scores[cfg] = mses[-1]\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Drop worst half\n",
    "    sorted_survivors = sorted(scores, key=scores.get)\n",
    "    keep = len(sorted_survivors) // 2\n",
    "    dropped = sorted_survivors[keep:]\n",
    "    survivors = sorted_survivors[:keep]\n",
    "\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f'Round {round_idx+1}: {budget} steps each\\nKeep: {[labels[c] for c in survivors]}', fontsize=9)\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel('Training steps', fontsize=9)\n",
    "    ax.legend(fontsize=7, ncol=2)\n",
    "    ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "    ax.set_ylim(0, 6)\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel('Validation MSE', fontsize=10)\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Hyperband (Successive Halving): Eliminate Bad Configs Early', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Final winner: {[labels[c] for c in survivors]}\")\n",
    "print(f\"True best config: {labels[np.argmin(true_final)]} (MSE={min(true_final):.2f})\")"
   ]
