    "## Summary — The Full Picture\n",
    "\n",
    "### Error decomposition\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\underbrace{\\mathbb{E}[(h_S(x)-y)^2]}_{\\text{Test error}} = \\underbrace{\\sigma^2}_{\\text{Irreducible}} + \\underbrace{(\\bar{h}(x)-h^*(x))^2}_{\\text{Bias}^2} + \\underbrace{\\mathbb{E}_S[(h_S(x)-\\bar{h}(x))^2]}_{\\text{Variance}}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### What controls each term\n",
    "\n",
    "| Error term | What changes it |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Noise $\\sigma^2$ | Data quality — irreducible without better sensors |\n",
    "| Bias² | Model expressiveness — richer class → lower bias |\n",
    "| Variance | Regularization, more data — reduces variance |\n",
    "\n",
    "### ML advice checklist\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "High train error?        → Bias problem → richer model, more features, less regularization\n",
    "Low train, high dev?     → Variance problem → more data, more regularization, simpler model\n",
    "Hyperparams not set?     → Use dev set + Hyperband, NOT test set\n",
    "Small dataset?           → Use K-fold cross-validation\n",
    "Large modern model?      → May be in double descent regime — don't panic\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Ridge regression reference\n",
    "\n",
    "| Formula | Meaning |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| $\\hat{\\theta} = (X^TX + \\rho I)^{-1}X^Ty$ | Closed-form ridge solution |\n",
    "| $\\rho = 0$ | Plain least squares |\n",
    "| $\\lambda_i \\to \\lambda_i + \\rho$ | Eigenvalue shift — bounds away from zero |\n",
    "| Bias cost | $\\hat{\\theta}$ shrunk toward zero |\n",
    "| Variance win | Inversion stable; model less sensitive to training set |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
